WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.655 line:82%
Here's Relay.

00:00:01.655 --> 00:00:09.220 line:82%
The idea is simple: let a model figure out a workflow once, then run
it again without asking the model.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.310 line:82%
Let's start with discovery.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:16.331 line:82%
I'm asking a local model to find a member's savings balance.

00:00:16.331 --> 00:00:21.492 line:82%
It reads the screen, chooses an allowed action, and checks what
happens next.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.420 line:82%
You can follow the steps here.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.580 line:82%
Search for the member, open their account, then read the balance.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:38.364 line:82%
Relay checks the member's identity and the final screen before it
saves anything as a successful workflow.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:49.922 line:82%
Here's what gets saved: a capability with inputs, outputs, and the
exact steps to repeat.

00:00:49.922 --> 00:00:54.468 line:82%
You can inspect it, export it, and test it before approving it.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.855 line:82%
Now let's try a different member.

00:00:58.855 --> 00:01:00.783 line:82%
Same capability, new input.

00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:04.280 line:82%
The saved steps run against the actual interface.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.492 line:82%
And here, you can see it used no model calls.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.755 line:82%
What if the member doesn't exist?

00:01:11.755 --> 00:01:14.284 line:82%
Relay returns a clear, known outcome.

00:01:14.284 --> 00:01:17.564 line:82%
It doesn't crash, or pretend the task succeeded.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.352 line:82%
Now the session has expired.

00:01:21.352 --> 00:01:24.195 line:82%
Relay pauses and tells me where it stopped.

00:01:24.195 --> 00:01:28.692 line:82%
I can take over this same session, with all the context still there.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.474 line:82%
I'll restore the session and hand control back.

00:01:33.474 --> 00:01:36.068 line:82%
Relay picks up from the interrupted step.

00:01:36.068 --> 00:01:38.852 line:82%
The timeline keeps a record of that handoff.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.312 line:82%
This also works with a second institution.

00:01:43.312 --> 00:01:49.740 line:82%
The interface is slightly different, but an explicit override lets us
reuse the same capability.

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:54.664 line:82%
And every run leaves evidence you can inspect.

00:01:54.664 --> 00:01:59.684 line:82%
That's Relay: learn the workflow, keep the contract, and stay in
control.
